      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define fraud indicators, escalation rules, and incident logging approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 544735,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Alright, moving on to T4. I've started a draft of the Fraud Indicators and Escalation Guideline in A4. I've listed some common ones like round-sum invoices and phantom employees. What other red flags have you encountered? We also need to define clear escalation thresholds.",
            "mentions": [
              505737,
              554843,
              235247,
              381305
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "Good list. I've seen cases with personal expenses being claimed as business costs. Also, invoices from companies that don't seem to exist.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 381305,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "What do we do if we see something suspicious? Do we tell the manager?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 554843,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "That's exactly what we need to define here. We need a clear, simple process. For example: if potential impact is < $1k, document and inform manager. If > $1k or it's a recurring pattern, we should have a formal escalation to the compliance officer.",
            "mentions": [
              381305
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "lightbulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 505737,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "I agree with that tiered approach. We should not investigate ourselves, just flag and escalate. The guideline in A4 needs to be explicit: 'Observe, Document, Escalate'. To support this, we need the incident log from T11. It should be a simple form: Client ID (anonymised), Date, Description of Indicator, and Clerk who flagged it. Nothing more, to keep it fast.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 544735,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I've updated A4 with the indicators mentioned and a two-tier escalation path: Level 1 (Inform Manager) for minor/isolated issues, and Level 2 (Formal Escalation to Compliance) for significant or systemic patterns. I've also drafted a simple incident log template based on your suggestion, @505737.",
            "mentions": [
              505737
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 235247,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "This is much clearer now. So we just fill out the log and send it to the manager or compliance? That's easy.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 505737,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Perfect. This looks robust but also practical. Let's get agreement on this. We confirm the final list of fraud indicators and the two-tier escalation steps as documented in A4. And we agree on the simple incident log format for T11, to be used for any Level 2 escalation. Any final thoughts or objections?",
            "mentions": [
